\[ \binom{52}{3} = \frac{52!}{3!(52-3)!} = \frac{52 \times 51 \times 50}{3 \times 2 \times 1} = 12870. \]

However, we are only interested in the number of ways to choose 3 cards from the 13 cards of each suit.  There are 4 suits, so the total number of ways to choose 3 cards from 4 suits is:

\[ 4 \times \binom{13}{3} = 4 \times \frac{13!}{3!(13-3)!} = 4 \times \frac{13 \times 12 \times 11}{3 \times 2 \times 1} = 1287. \]

Therefore, the number of ways to choose 3 cards from a standard deck of 52 cards, if all three cards must be of different suits, is \boxed{1287}.

